::ALG2_U02_L08_GP01::
Question ID: ALG2_U02_L08_GP01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.PF.8
Question:
Which polynomial has both ends rising?
{
=A. f(x) \= 2x⁴ - x + 1#Correct. Even degree and positive leading coefficient make both ends rise.
~B. f(x) \= -2x⁴ + 1#Even degree with a negative leading coefficient makes both ends fall.
~C. f(x) \= x³ - 1#Odd degree has opposite end behavior.
~D. f(x) \= -x³ + 1#Odd degree has opposite end behavior.
}

::ALG2_U02_L08_GP02::
Question ID: ALG2_U02_L08_GP02
MLA Standard: Support-only review; no new primary MLA standard
Question:
What does an even multiplicity zero usually do on a graph?
{
~A. The graph crosses the x-axis.#Crossing is typical of odd multiplicity.
=B. The graph touches and turns at the x-axis.#Correct. Even multiplicity commonly causes a bounce.
~C. The graph has no x-intercept.#A zero is an x-intercept when it is real.
~D. The graph becomes linear.#Multiplicity does not make the whole graph linear.
}

::ALG2_U02_L08_GP03::
Question ID: ALG2_U02_L08_GP03
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.PF.4
Question:
A quadratic model has vertex (3, -5) and opens upward. What is the minimum value?
{
~A. 3#The x-coordinate gives where the minimum occurs.
~B. -3#This is not the y-value of the vertex.
=C. -5#Correct. The y-coordinate of the vertex is the minimum value.
~D. 5#The sign of the y-value matters.
}

::ALG2_U02_L08_GP04::
Question ID: ALG2_U02_L08_GP04
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.PF.2
Question:
Which interval solves x² - 4 >= 0?
{
~A. -2 <\= x <\= 2#That is where the graph is on or below the x-axis.
~B. -2 < x < 2#This interval excludes zeros and has the wrong sign.
~C. all real numbers#The graph is negative between the zeros.
=D. x <\= -2 or x >\= 2#Correct. The graph is on or above the x-axis outside the zeros.
}

::ALG2_U02_L08_GP05::
Question ID: ALG2_U02_L08_GP05
MLA Standard: Support-only application; no new primary MLA standard
Question:
A polynomial model has an x-intercept at 6 hours. What can that mean in context?
{
~A. The model is always increasing after 6 hours.#An intercept does not guarantee increasing behavior.
=B. The output quantity is 0 at 6 hours.#Correct. An x-intercept means the function value is 0.
~C. The maximum value is 6.#An x-intercept is not necessarily a maximum.
~D. The leading coefficient is 6.#An intercept does not identify the leading coefficient.
}

